{"content":[{"c":["MYSIA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Region in northwest Asia Minor (modern Turkey). It had a long history, leading up to its annexation into the Roman Empire in 133 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," as part of the province of Asia. For about 150 years before that it had been part of the kingdom of Pergamum. The travel account in ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.16.7-8","r":"Acts.16.7-8","rawR":"Acts.16.7-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.16.7-8","value":"Acts.16.7-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 16:7-8"}," indicates that the apostle Paul passed through this region on his second missionary journey but did not preach there."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=PergamosPergamum_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"PergamosPergamum_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"PergamosPergamum_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Pergamos, Pergamum"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Mysia","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Acts 16:7-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.16.7-8","rawQueryValue":"Acts.16.7-8","sourceRefExact":"Acts.16.7-8"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"df81676c94c1530d44aebbd24877ffafb58ad82b1c30e1129b2f77829029a51f","sourceItemName":"Mysia","sourceItemOrder":448,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Mysia","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Mysia","title":"Mysia","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}